direct_io.zig, tool_parse.zig and tool_parse_test.zig are TensorFold's own later versions (commits e561a257 and
c126fe16: a test's reference read, and GLM tool calls read when the model drops an <arg_key> or the end token leaves
a value open), taken in unchanged apart from their first line; Fiore-lab then changed tool_parse.zig and
tool_parse_test.zig so that a GLM value holding </arg_value> or </tool_call> reads whole (glm_rescue.zig).

zig/src/core/lanes/sampling_ref.zig is TensorFold 1.0.2's zig/src/core/lanes/sampling.zig, unchanged apart from its
first two lines: the reference zig/src/core/lanes/sampling_match_test.zig and
zig/src/expertatlas/sampling_match_test.zig check the better C samplers against.

Fiore-lab's published tree leaves out TensorFold's documents; its README*.md (English, Japanese, Simplified Chinese
and Korean), packaging/RUNTIME*.md (English, Japanese and Simplified Chinese) and the documents under glm53/ are
Fiore-lab's, and Fiore-lab added the sections "Full GLM-5.3 in Zig" and "Unicode data" to THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The published tree also leaves out the parts of TensorFold 1.0.2 that Expert Atlas's own build does not build: the
families other than glm_moe_dsa, the Metal backend and kernels, the CUDA kernels other than zig/kernels/cuda/glm53/,
the lane host (except zig/src/core/lanes/sampling_ref.zig, the reference Expert Atlas's sampler is checked against)
with the lanes' keyed sampler in better C, the cluster and fabric layers, TensorFold's CLI, engine registries and CUDA
build, and their tests and tools. Of the changed files listed above, tools/zig/test_lanes.sh, zig/build/cuda.zig,
zig/src/core/engine_api.zig, zig/src/core/lane_host_reuse_test.zig, zig/src/core/lanes/sampling.zig,
zig/src/native/cuda.zig, zig/tests/server/build.sh and zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh are among them, and so is
zig/build/lanes.zig of the additions. Its THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md keeps the sections for what it holds.

The additions include code from TensorFold's Python engine and from b12x, some of it
modified by Fiore-lab, as THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists. The additions are licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. What they take from
other projects is listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md under "Full GLM-5.3 in Zig".
